# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/region_streets.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event streets_sea_fog
# en: The Sea Fog
title [c5b7c3] = 海雾
# en: A sea fog rolls up the river and swallows the capital whole. The lamplighters come out hours early; carriages crawl with men walking at the horses' heads; the bells sound like they're ringing underwater. At a corner an old man with a white stick is standing quite still. "I know these streets blind," he says. "But not like this. Nobody does."
text [f36d5b] = 一场海雾顺着河涌上来，把整个王都吞了进去。点灯人提早了几个钟头出来点灯；马车慢慢爬，车夫走在马头前面牵着；钟声听起来像在水底下敲。街角站着一个拄白手杖的老人，一动不动。“这些街我闭着眼都认得，”他说，“可不是这样的街。谁也认不得。”
# en: A city street swallowed by thick white sea fog, lamps lit, figures looming out of the mist, a student guiding an old blind man by the arm.
scene [31476f] = 城市街道被浓密的白色海雾吞没，灯都点着，人影从雾中浮现，一个学生挽着一位盲眼老人的胳膊引路。
# en: Walk him home through the fog
opt.left.label [e0a53b] = 在雾里送他回家
# en: He knows the way by the sound of things: the bakery's oven door, the drip of a certain gutter, a parrot in a window. You're his eyes for traffic and he's yours for everything else. It takes two hours. At his door he gives you a toffee, and you walk back through the fog chilled to the bone.
opt.left.say.1 [951c06] = 他靠声音认路：面包房的炉门、某条水沟的滴水声、窗户里的一只鹦鹉。你替他看车，他替你认别的一切。走了两个钟头。到了他家门口，他给了你一块太妃糖，你在雾里走回去，冷到了骨头里。
# en: Wait it out in a coffee house
opt.right.label [b807e9] = 进咖啡馆等雾散
# en: You duck into a coffee house where half the street has had the same idea, and spend the fog, and a few coppers, in a fug of coffee and strangers' stories. When it lifts the city looks washed, and nobody wants to leave.
opt.right.say.1 [829b1e] = 你钻进一家咖啡馆，半条街的人都打了同样的主意，你在咖啡的热气和陌生人的故事里熬过了这场雾，花了几个铜板。雾散了，城市像洗过一样，谁都不想走。

@event streets_balloon
# en: The Ascent
title [6bc84a] = 升空
# en: An aeronaut in goggles has a great striped balloon tethered in a square in midtown, swelling over the crowd, and he's selling places in the basket for one ascent on a rope, as high as the cathedral's spire and back down. "Only the brave," he shouts. "Or the rich. Ideally both."
text [2fbea8] = 一个戴护目镜的气球驾驶员在中城一个广场上拴着一只条纹大气球，气球在人群上方鼓胀起来，他在卖篮子里的位置：拴着绳子升一次，高到大教堂的尖顶再下来。“只限勇敢的人，”他喊，“或者有钱的人。最好两样都占。”
# en: A great striped hot-air balloon tethered in a city square, a crowd watching, an aeronaut in goggles selling places in the basket, a student at the rope barrier.
scene [a065b9] = 城市广场上拴着一只巨大的条纹热气球，人群围观，一个戴护目镜的气球驾驶员在卖篮子里的位置，一个学生站在绳栏边。
# en: Buy a place in the basket
opt.left.label [cee349] = 买个篮子里的位置
# en: The ground lets go of you all at once. Up and up, past the chimneys, past the bells, until the whole capital lies under you like a map, the river a silver thread to the sea. The basket creaks. Nobody speaks. You'll remember it all your life.
opt.left.say.1 [b61a8f] = 你付了钱，大地一下子放开了你。往上，再往上，越过烟囱，越过钟楼，直到整个王都像一张地图铺在你脚下，河是一条通往大海的银线。篮子吱呀作响。谁也不说话。你会记一辈子。
# en: Hold a guy-rope for the aeronaut
opt.right.label [79564c] = 替驾驶员拉一根稳绳
# en: He's short a rope-hand, and you spend the ascent leaning back on a guy-rope with three porters while the balloon tugs at you like a kite the size of a church. Your hands are rope-burned. The aeronaut lets you keep his spare goggles.
opt.right.say.1 [4efe5f] = 他缺一个拉绳的人，于是升空的整个过程你都和三个搬运工一起往后仰着拽一根稳绳，气球像一只教堂那么大的风筝一样拉扯着你。你的手被绳子磨破了。驾驶员把他备用的护目镜送给了你。

@event streets_ballad_seller
# en: A Song About the Academy
title [5bfdfd] = 一首关于学院的歌
# en: On a street corner a ballad-seller is singing the latest broadside, a penny a sheet, to a laughing crowd. It's about your academy: a hundred verses of wizards in towers, a lake with a monster in it, and a headmistress who eats students who are late. The crowd wants to know if it's true. Several of them are looking at your scarf.
text [4fd71f] = 街角一个卖唱本的在唱最新的单页歌谣，一便士一张，一群人围着笑。唱的是你的学院：一百段歌词，塔楼里的巫师、湖里的怪物，还有一个吃掉迟到学生的校长。人群想知道是不是真的。好几个人在看你的围巾。
# en: A busy city corner, a ballad-seller in a battered hat singing from a sheet with more sheets pegged on a string behind him, a crowd laughing, a student listening with folded arms.
scene [3a597a] = 繁忙的城市街角，一个戴破帽子的卖唱本的照着单子唱歌，身后绳子上夹着更多唱本，人群在笑，一个学生抱着胳膊在听。
# en: Buy a sheet and sing the chorus
opt.left.label [783574] = 买一张，跟着唱副歌
# en: You buy a sheet, learn the chorus and sing it back at him louder. The crowd roars. By evening the ballad has a new verse, about a student with a scarf who sings out of tune, and it sells better than ever.
opt.left.say.1 [0eb85e] = 你花一便士买了一张，学会副歌，冲他唱得更响。人群哄笑叫好。到傍晚这首歌多了一段新词，唱一个戴围巾、唱歌跑调的学生，卖得比以前还好。
# en: Ask him where he got it
opt.right.label [cead71] = 问他歌是哪儿来的
# en: Between songs he tells you: from a printer's devil, who had it from a sailor, whose cousin was at the academy for one term and left in a hurry. "Every verse is true somewhere," he says. You walk on wondering which verse the cousin ran from, and can't shake it all day.
opt.right.say.1 [9620ef] = 两首歌之间他告诉你：从一个印刷学徒那儿来的，学徒是从一个水手那儿听的，水手的表亲在学院读过一个学期，走得很匆忙。“每段词在什么地方都是真的，”他说。你走开时一直在想那个表亲是从哪段词里逃出来的，一整天都甩不掉这个念头。

@event streets_chimney_fire
# en: Fire in the Chimney
title [968d38] = 烟囱起火
# en: Smoke and then flame come out of a chimney in a crowded street, and in a moment the whole street is out with buckets. The pump's at the far end; the chain is too short; sparks are falling on the next roof. Somebody spots your academy scarf and shouts, "Wizard!" as if it were an instruction.
text [767171] = 拥挤的街上一根烟囱先冒烟，接着冒火，眨眼间整条街的人都提着桶出来了。水泵在街那头；传桶的队伍太短；火星正落到隔壁屋顶上。有人看见你的学院围巾，喊了一声“巫师！”，好像那是一道命令。
# en: A narrow city street with smoke and flame pouring from a chimney stack, neighbours forming a bucket chain from a pump, a student running towards it.
scene [986d9d] = 狭窄的城市街道，一根烟囱里涌出浓烟和火焰，邻居们从水泵排起传桶的队伍，一个学生朝那边跑去。
# en: Join the bucket chain
opt.left.label [a4709d] = 加入传桶的队伍
# en: You take your place in the chain and pass buckets till your arms shake and your sleeves are soaked. The fire goes out in the chimney before it gets to the roof. A woman with a soot-blackened face brings everybody tea. Your hands are blistered from the handles.
opt.left.say.1 [bb2a46] = 你在队伍里站好，一桶接一桶地传，直到胳膊发抖、袖子湿透。火在烧到屋顶之前在烟囱里灭了。一个满脸烟灰的女人给每个人端来了茶。桶把手把你的手磨出了水泡。
# en: Smother it with a spell
opt.right.label [fae783] = 用咒语把火闷灭
# en: You stand in the street and close your hand, and the fire in the chimney goes out like a snuffed candle. The street cheers. The sweep, arriving late, is furious, and the householder kisses you on both cheeks.
opt.right.say.1 [48c359] = 你站在街上把手一握，烟囱里的火就像被掐灭的蜡烛一样熄了。整条街欢呼起来。来晚了的扫烟囱的气坏了，房主在你两边脸颊上各亲了一下。
# en: Your spell meets the fire and makes it angrier, and a gout of soot comes down the street like a black wave. The bucket chain puts it out. You're black from head to foot and coughing, and nobody's quite sure whose side you were on.
opt.right.say.2 [fb852e] = 你的咒语撞上火，反倒把它激怒了，一股烟灰像黑浪一样涌下街道。传桶的队伍把火扑灭了。你从头黑到脚，咳个不停，谁也说不准你到底帮的是哪一边。

@event streets_omnibus
# en: On Top of the Omnibus
title [87f88a] = 公共马车顶上
# en: The horse omnibus crosses the whole capital for a penny, uptown to Port Calder, and the best seats are on the open roof, where the wind is and the gossip is. Today the roof is full: clerks, a fishwife, a curate, and one seat left between two people arguing about coal. On the stair behind you a tired woman with a basket of eggs is looking at it too.
text [bfe39a] = 马拉公共马车一便士就能横穿整个王都，从上城到考尔德港，最好的座位在敞开的车顶上，那里有风，也有闲话。今天车顶坐满了：职员、卖鱼的女人、一个副牧师，只剩一个座位，夹在两个为煤价吵架的人中间。你身后的楼梯上，一个提着一篮鸡蛋、满脸疲惫的女人也在看着那个座位。
# en: The open top deck of a horse-drawn omnibus crossing a city, passengers on benches, a student squeezed between a clerk and a woman with a basket of eggs, rooftops passing.
scene [e53984] = 马拉公共马车敞开的上层，乘客坐在长凳上，一个学生挤在一个职员和一个提着一篮鸡蛋的女人之间，屋顶从旁掠过。
# en: Take the last seat and listen
opt.left.label [9954f8] = 坐最后那个座位，听着
# en: You pay your penny and ride the whole route with your elbows in, while the city goes past and the roof argues about coal, the war, a duke's divorce and whether wizards should pay tax. You learn the capital from top to bottom, and you're very, very squashed.
opt.left.say.1 [fea9a7] = 你付了一便士，缩着胳膊肘坐完了全程，城市从身边经过，车顶上在吵煤价、战争、一位公爵的离婚，还有巫师该不该交税。你从上到下认识了王都，也被挤得非常、非常扁。
# en: Give her the seat, and walk
opt.right.label [1bb873] = 把座位让给她，自己走
# en: You hand the egg-woman up to the last seat and walk the route instead, keeping up with the horses on every hill. She tells the whole roof you're a credit to your mother. You arrive in Port Calder footsore, with your penny still in your pocket.
opt.right.say.1 [1dc4b9] = 你把提鸡蛋的女人扶上最后一个座位，自己跟着马车走完全程，每个上坡都得追上马。她逢人就跟整个车顶说你是你母亲的骄傲。你到考尔德港时脚都走疼了，一便士还在兜里。

@event streets_preacher
# en: The Preacher Against Wizards
title [6a5ff3] = 反对巫师的布道者
# en: In a square a street preacher on a box is warning the crowd against wizards: they bend the world out of true, he says, they answer to nobody, they take the light of the Lamp and use it for their own ends. Then he sees your scarf, and points. "Ask that one," he says. "Ask what they're learning up there in their castle."
text [98096c] = 广场上一个站在箱子上的街头布道者在告诫人群提防巫师：他说他们把世界掰歪了，他们不对任何人负责，他们拿了明灯的光去办自己的事。接着他看见了你的围巾，伸手一指。“问问那个人，”他说，“问问他们在城堡里学些什么。”
# en: A city square, a fervent street preacher on a box with a lantern, a small crowd listening, a student in an academy scarf at the edge of the crowd being pointed at.
scene [83eb88] = 城市广场上，一个狂热的街头布道者提着灯站在箱子上，一小群人在听，人群边上一个戴学院围巾的学生正被人指着。
# en: Answer him in front of the crowd
opt.left.label [08d8fe] = 当着人群回答他
# en: You step up and answer him honestly: you're learning to mend, to ward, to keep a fever down. Some of what he fears is real. Most of it is lessons. The crowd listens, and when you finish the preacher, to everyone's surprise, shakes your hand.
opt.left.say.1 [e116e7] = 你走上前，诚实地回答他：你在学怎么治伤、怎么设护盾、怎么退烧。他害怕的东西有一些是真的。大部分只是功课。人群听着，你说完时，出乎所有人意料，布道者跟你握了手。
# en: You answer him, and he has a reply for every word, and the crowd likes his better. You walk away with your scarf feeling very bright and the square's eyes on your back.
opt.left.say.2 [e27058] = 你回答他，可你说一句他有一句等着，人群更喜欢他的说法。你走开时觉得围巾亮得刺眼，背后全是广场上的目光。
# en: Walk on
opt.right.label [383259] = 走开
# en: You walk on with your face hot. Behind you the preacher tells the crowd that's how they always are, and some of them agree, and you think about it the rest of the day.
opt.right.say.1 [5ee530] = 你红着脸走开了。身后布道者对人群说他们向来就是这副样子，有些人点头称是，你一整天都在想这件事。

@event streets_flower_seller
# en: Hothouse Violets
title [aeeaa8] = 温室紫罗兰
# en: On a street corner an old flower seller is unloading baskets of hothouse violets from the last market cart of the morning, too slowly, and the carter is shouting that he has six more streets to do. The violets smell of spring, whatever the month. She looks up at you, and then at the baskets, and doesn't ask.
text [2c4656] = 街角一个卖花的老妇人正从上午最后一辆市场车上卸一篮篮温室紫罗兰，卸得太慢了，赶车的嚷着说他还有六条街要送。紫罗兰闻起来像春天，不管眼下是几月。她抬头看看你，又看看那些篮子，没有开口。
# en: A city street corner at midday, an old flower seller in a shawl with baskets of violets, a heavy flower cart half-unloaded, a student stopping.
scene [308028] = 正午的城市街角，一个裹着披肩的卖花老妇人守着一篮篮紫罗兰，一辆沉重的花车卸了一半，一个学生停下脚步。
# en: Unload the cart for her
opt.left.label [27ac99] = 帮她卸车
# en: You carry her baskets down from the cart, eight of them, wet and heavy, while the carter drums his fingers. She gives you a bunch of violets for your trouble and a blessing in a language you don't know. Your back aches and your coat smells of violets all day.
opt.left.say.1 [e93960] = 你替她把篮子从车上搬下来，八篮，又湿又沉，赶车的在一旁敲着手指。她送你一束紫罗兰作为辛苦钱，还用一种你不懂的语言给了你一句祝福。你的腰酸了，外套一整天都是紫罗兰的味道。
# en: Buy a bunch of violets
opt.right.label [2cb59f] = 买一束紫罗兰
# en: You buy a bunch for a penny, and she wraps them in a twist of newspaper. You carry them about all day and they make every room you walk into smell like spring.
opt.right.say.1 [409962] = 你花一便士买了一束，她用一卷报纸包好。你带着它走了一整天，走进哪个房间，哪个房间就闻起来像春天。

@event streets_downpour
# en: Under the Same Awning
title [cf587a] = 同一个雨篷下
# en: The heavens open over midtown, and a dozen strangers run for the same shop awning: a soldier, two seamstresses, a man with a cello case, a very wet dog. The rain shows no sign of stopping. The man with the cello case looks at the others, and at his case, and at you, and says, "Well. We might as well."
text [944fd6] = 中城上空突然大雨倾盆，十几个陌生人跑到同一个店铺的雨篷下：一个士兵、两个女裁缝、一个背大提琴盒的男人、一条湿透的狗。雨一点没有要停的意思。背大提琴盒的男人看看其他人，看看琴盒，又看看你，说：“好吧。那就来吧。”
# en: A sudden city downpour, rain bouncing off the cobbles, a crowd of strangers sheltering under a shop awning, a student among them.
scene [780239] = 城市突降大雨，雨点在鹅卵石上弹跳，一群陌生人挤在店铺雨篷下避雨，一个学生在其中。
# en: Stay and listen
opt.left.label [465e74] = 留下来听
# en: He takes out the cello and plays under the awning while the rain comes down, and the seamstresses sing, and the soldier knows the words. The dog howls along on the high notes. Everyone drops a coin in his open case, and so do you. It's still raining an hour later, and nobody wants it to stop.
opt.left.say.1 [1c1155] = 他拿出大提琴，在雨篷下拉了起来，雨哗哗地下，女裁缝们唱，士兵也会词。狗在高音处跟着嚎。人人都往他打开的琴盒里丢了一枚硬币，你也丢了。一个钟头后还在下雨，谁也不想让它停。
# en: Run for it through the rain
opt.right.label [b7eb8a] = 冒雨跑回去
# en: You run for it, through rivers in the gutters and rain like thrown gravel, and arrive at your door soaked to the skin and laughing. Behind you, faintly, a cello starts to play.
opt.right.say.1 [2794d6] = 你冒雨跑了，蹚过水沟里的小河，雨点像扔过来的碎石，到门口时浑身湿透，笑个不停。你身后，隐约地，一把大提琴开始拉了起来。

@event streets_automaton
# en: The Writing Automaton
title [595132] = 写字的自动人偶
# en: A crowd has gathered at a clockmaker's window, where a brass automaton in a velvet coat sits at a little desk and writes with a real quill, a new line every hour. People wait all day to see what it writes. As you press closer the brass head turns, slowly, towards the glass, and the quill begins to move.
text [e3e296] = 一家钟表店的橱窗外围了一群人，橱窗里一个穿天鹅绒外套的黄铜自动人偶坐在小书桌前，用一支真正的羽毛笔写字，每小时写一行。人们等上一整天，就为看它写什么。你挤近时，那颗黄铜脑袋慢慢地转向玻璃，羽毛笔动了起来。
# en: A clockmaker's shop window with a crowd outside, a brass automaton boy at a tiny desk writing with a quill, a student pressed close to the glass.
scene [fe1dae] = 钟表店橱窗外围着一群人，一个黄铜自动人偶男孩坐在小书桌前用羽毛笔写字，一个学生紧贴着玻璃。
# en: Wait to read what it writes
opt.left.label [c39a44] = 等着看它写什么
# en: It writes, in a beautiful copperplate hand, "Good day," and then a word you don't know, and then, quite clearly, your initials. The crowd turns to look at you. The clockmaker insists it writes random letters. You don't sleep well.
opt.left.say.1 [90a262] = 它用漂亮的铜版体写下“日安”，然后是一个你不认识的词，然后，清清楚楚地，是你的姓名首字母。人群转过来看你。钟表匠坚持说它写的是随机的字母。你没睡好。
# en: Ask the clockmaker how it works
opt.right.label [56e6a2] = 问钟表匠它是怎么做的
# en: The clockmaker shows you the back of it for a penny: four hundred cams, a drum of brass pegs, and no magic whatsoever, he swears. You spot one cam that isn't brass. He sees you see it, and closes the case, and offers you a peppermint.
opt.right.say.1 [f174cc] = 钟表匠收你一便士，给你看它的背面：四百个凸轮，一个插满黄铜销钉的鼓，他发誓一点魔法都没有。你发现有一个凸轮不是黄铜的。他看见你看见了，关上了箱子，递给你一颗薄荷糖。

@event streets_procession
# en: The Royal Coach
title [5d6ba1] = 御驾
# en: The avenue is packed for the royal coach, which goes from the palace to the cathedral twice a year for no reason anybody can remember, with outriders, trumpets and a great deal of gilt. Children are on shoulders, old men on boxes, and the only free view is from the top of a lamp-post.
text [00d27d] = 大道上挤满了等御驾的人，御驾一年两次从王宫去大教堂，谁也记不清为什么，有骑马的侍从、号手和大量镀金。孩子骑在肩上，老人站在箱子上，唯一不用挤的视野在一根灯柱顶上。
# en: A broad city avenue lined with cheering crowds and flags, a gilded royal coach with outriders passing, a student up on a lamp-post above the crowd.
scene [5e2abe] = 宽阔的城市大道两旁挤满欢呼的人群和旗帜，一辆镀金的御用马车在侍从护卫下经过，一个学生爬在人群上方的灯柱上。
# en: Climb the lamp-post
opt.left.label [0c586a] = 爬上灯柱
# en: You shin up the lamp-post as the trumpets sound and see the whole procession go by beneath you, plumes and gilt and a pale royal hand at the coach window that, you'd swear, waves at you. The crowd below cheers you down.
opt.left.say.1 [4adef3] = 号角响起时你顺着灯柱爬了上去，看着整支队伍从脚下经过，羽饰和镀金，马车窗口一只苍白的王室之手，你敢发誓，是在向你挥。底下的人群欢呼着把你迎了下来。
# en: You get halfway up the lamp-post and slide down it with your arms round it, burning your palms, just as the coach goes past. You see a wheel. It's a very fine wheel.
opt.left.say.2 [1cf43a] = 你爬到灯柱一半，抱着它滑了下来，手掌磨得火辣辣的，正好御驾经过。你看见了一个车轮。是个非常漂亮的车轮。
# en: Watch the crowd for pickpockets
opt.right.label [558951] = 在人群里盯扒手
# en: You don't watch the coach. You watch the crowd, and spot three pickpockets working the edge, and stand very obviously beside each of their marks until they give up. You miss the whole procession, and feel quietly useful.
opt.right.say.1 [360679] = 你没看御驾。你看人群，发现有三个扒手在边上下手，于是挨个站到他们的目标身边，站得明明白白，直到他们放弃。整支队伍你一眼没看到，心里却悄悄觉得自己有用。

@event lanes_carrier
# en: The Carrier's Cart
title [28cdd4] = 运货人的车
# en: The valley carrier comes up behind you on the lane, his cart piled with hampers, a coffin-shaped parcel and a crate of very indignant geese. "Going my way?" he says. "Everybody is, there's only the one road. Hop on the tail. Mind the geese. Or, if you're walking anyhow, there's a parcel for the farm at the top that's a day late."
text [8cf285] = 山谷里的运货人赶着车从小路上追上你，车上堆着食篮、一个棺材形状的包裹，还有一笼非常愤慨的鹅。“顺路吗？”他说，“人人都顺路，就这一条路。跳到车尾上来。当心那些鹅。要不，你反正要走路的话，有个给山顶农场的包裹，已经晚了一天了。”
# en: A slow carrier's cart on a country lane piled with hampers, parcels and a crate of indignant geese, a stout carrier on the box offering a student a lift.
scene [0dc9c3] = 乡间小路上一辆慢吞吞的运货车，堆满食篮、包裹和一笼愤慨的鹅，一个矮壮的运货人坐在车座上，招呼一个学生搭车。
# en: Ride on the tail, minding the geese
opt.left.label [e40d9d] = 坐在车尾，看着那些鹅
# en: You ride the tailboard with your feet dangling and the geese hissing at your back, the whole valley going past at a walking pace. Somewhere past the mill the biggest goose gets your ear through the slats. The carrier says it's a sign she likes you.
opt.left.say.1 [d57129] = 你坐在车尾板上晃着脚，鹅在你背后嘶嘶叫，整个山谷以步行的速度从身边经过。过了磨坊不远，最大的那只鹅隔着板条叼住了你的耳朵。运货人说这说明她喜欢你。
# en: Carry the late parcel up
opt.right.label [1ffcf3] = 把晚了的包裹送上去
# en: You carry the parcel up the long hill to the top farm, where the farmer's wife opens it on the step: a new teapot, in one piece. She gives you a coin and a slice of seed cake, and makes you drink the first cup out of it, sitting on the step with a stitch in your side.
opt.right.say.1 [7c5c68] = 你扛着包裹爬上长长的山坡，送到山顶农场，农夫的妻子在台阶上拆开：一把新茶壶，完好无损。她给了你一枚硬币和一片葛缕子蛋糕，还非让你用它倒的第一杯茶，你坐在台阶上喝着，岔着气。

@event lanes_flock
# en: The Flock in the Lane
title [edc073] = 小路上的羊群
# en: The lane is suddenly full of sheep, three hundred of them, wall to wall, being moved down from the upland by a young shepherd and a black-and-white dog who are both doing all the work. You're in the middle of the flock. The shepherd waves his crook at you, either hello or get out of the way.
text [60231f] = 小路上突然挤满了羊，三百只，从这边墙挤到那边墙，一个年轻的牧羊人和一条黑白花的狗正把它们从高地赶下来，活全是这两个干的。你被困在羊群中间。牧羊人冲你挥了挥牧羊杖，要么是打招呼，要么是让你让开。
# en: A narrow country lane completely filled with a flock of sheep, a young shepherd and a black-and-white dog working them, a student stuck in the middle.
scene [e4953a] = 一条被羊群完全塞满的狭窄乡间小路，一个年轻的牧羊人和一条黑白花的牧羊犬在赶羊，一个学生被困在中间。
# en: Help turn them at the gate
opt.left.label [8d4588] = 帮着把羊赶进门
# en: The dog does the clever part and you do the running about with your arms out, which the sheep ignore until, suddenly, they don't. They pour through the gate like water. The shepherd laughs at you, kindly, and the dog doesn't look at you at all.
opt.left.say.1 [5ce084] = 聪明的活儿狗干了，你负责张着胳膊到处跑，羊根本不理你，直到突然之间，它们理了。羊像水一样涌进门。牧羊人笑你，笑得很和善，狗压根没看你一眼。
# en: Stand still and let them flow past
opt.right.label [7f5da9] = 站着不动，让它们流过去
# en: You stand very still and the flock parts round you like a river round a stone, three hundred woolly backs and the smell of lanolin, for ten whole minutes. By the end you've forgotten what you were walking somewhere to do.
opt.right.say.1 [c6ac0d] = 你站得一动不动，羊群像河水绕过石头一样从你身边分开流过，三百个毛茸茸的背和羊毛脂的气味，整整十分钟。到最后你已经忘了自己本来要走去干什么。

@event lanes_wedding
# en: A Wedding on the Road
title [178c64] = 路上的婚礼
# en: A wedding party is coming down the lane from the chapel, bride and groom in flower crowns, a fiddler in front, half the village dancing behind. You stand aside to let them pass. You're not allowed to. The bride's grandmother takes you by both hands. {at_home(): "Home for a wedding and standing in a hedge?" she says. "Dance."|"A stranger at a wedding is good luck," she says. "Dance."}
text [33f61f] = 一支婚礼队伍正从礼拜堂沿小路走下来，新郎新娘戴着花冠，前面一个提琴手，半个村子跳着舞跟在后面。你站到一边让他们过。他们不许。新娘的祖母抓住你的两只手。{at_home(): “回家赶上婚礼，倒站在树篱边上？”她说，“跳吧。”|“婚礼上来个外乡人是好兆头，”她说，“跳吧。”}
# en: A country wedding procession on a lane, a bride and groom with flower crowns, a fiddler, villagers dancing, one of them pulling a student into the dance.
scene [065dc0] = 小路上的乡村婚礼队伍，新郎新娘戴着花冠，一个提琴手，村民们在跳舞，其中一人把一个学生拉进舞圈。
# en: Dance with the wedding
opt.left.label [453067] = 跟着婚礼跳舞
# en: You dance the length of the lane and three times round the green, and are fed cake and cider and kissed by a great many aunts. Your feet are wrecked. Somebody tucks a flower from the bride's crown into your buttonhole for luck.
opt.left.say.1 [252a29] = 你跳完了整条小路，又绕着草地跳了三圈，被喂了蛋糕和苹果酒，被许许多多的姑妈亲了脸。你的脚彻底废了。有人从新娘的花冠上取下一朵花，别进你的扣眼，说是图个吉利。
# en: Give the couple a gift and go
opt.right.label [fd8b2d] = 送新人一份礼，然后离开
# en: You press a coin into the groom's hand for luck, as the custom is, and the bride laughs and gives you a flower in exchange. The fiddler plays you a few bars down the lane as you go, and you hear it a long way.
opt.right.say.1 [4193c2] = 你照习俗往新郎手里塞了一枚硬币图个吉利，新娘笑着回赠你一朵花。你沿小路走开时，提琴手为你拉了几小节，你走出好远还听得见。

@event lanes_thunderstorm
# en: Storm Over the Valley
title [37477e] = 山谷上空的雷暴
# en: A summer thunderstorm comes over the valley, black as a bruise, and the lightning goes straight for the ridge. You run for the nearest barn. Inside there are cows, warm and unbothered. Outside, the lightning keeps striking the standing stones up on the ridge, one after another, as if it were counting them.
text [5d6f04] = 一场夏日雷暴压过山谷，黑得像一块瘀青，闪电直奔山脊而去。你跑向最近的谷仓。里面有牛，暖和，满不在乎。外面，闪电一下接一下地劈在山脊的立石上，一块接一块，好像在数它们。
# en: A wide valley under a towering thunderstorm, lightning striking the ridge's standing stones, a student sheltering in the doorway of a stone barn with cows inside.
scene [976d22] = 宽阔的山谷上空耸立着雷暴云，闪电劈在山脊的立石上，一个学生躲在一座石砌谷仓门口，里面有牛。
# en: Watch the stones from the doorway
opt.left.label [15dcb1] = 在门口看那些石头
# en: You count the strikes. The lightning hits every stone on the ridge, once each, in order. When it's done, the storm goes over as if it had finished a job. You walk home past the ridge in the clean air and don't look up at it. You're on edge all evening.
opt.left.say.1 [cbd811] = 你数着雷击。闪电把山脊上每一块石头都劈了一次，按着顺序。劈完了，暴风雨就过去了，像干完了一件活。你在清新的空气里经过山脊走回去，没有抬头看。你一整晚都心神不宁。
# en: Sit with the cows until it passes
opt.right.label [ebe080] = 跟牛待在一起等它过去
# en: You sit in the straw with the cows, who are entirely unbothered, and eat the apples you were saving, and listen to the rain on the slates. When it's over you're damp and smell of cow, and quite peaceful.
opt.right.say.1 [14256d] = 你坐在干草里和牛待在一起，它们毫不在意，你吃掉了留着的苹果，听雨打在石板瓦上。等雨停了，你潮乎乎的，一身牛味，心里却很平静。

@event lanes_milestone
# en: To the Hill, Seven
title [6394f3] = 往山，七
# en: At a fork in the lane there's an old milestone, mossy and leaning, carved with distances. One arm says the market village, two. The other says the mill, three. And a third face, half under the moss, says only TO THE HILL, VII, and points at a field with no gate, towards the moors.
text [c389f5] = 小路的岔口立着一块长满青苔、歪斜的老里程碑，刻着里程。一面写着集镇，二。另一面写着磨坊，三。第三面一半埋在青苔下，只写着往山，七，指向一片没有门的田，朝着荒原的方向。
# en: An old mossy milestone at a fork in a country lane, carved with worn directions, a student crouching to read it, the lane forking away into mist.
scene [b952fd] = 乡间小路岔口一块长满青苔的老里程碑，刻着磨损的方向，一个学生蹲着辨认，小路分岔延伸进雾里。
# en: Walk a little way that way
opt.left.label [e05218] = 朝那边走一小段
# en: You climb the stile into the field and walk towards nothing in particular. Seven fields on there's a hedge too thick to pass, and over it the hill on the moors, much nearer than it has any right to be. You go back to the road, and it's back where it belongs. Your skin prickles all the way back.
opt.left.say.1 [e049a1] = 你翻过踏阶进了田，漫无目的地往前走。走过七片田，有一道密得过不去的树篱，越过它望去，是荒原上的那座山，近得毫无道理。你回到路上，山又回到了它该在的地方。你一路上心里发毛。
# en: Clear the moss and copy it down
opt.right.label [0c696a] = 清掉青苔，把它抄下来
# en: You scrape the moss off with your thumbnail and copy the old letters into your notebook. Under TO THE HILL someone has scratched a later line, very small: NOT THIS YEAR. Your thumbnail is torn.
opt.right.say.1 [9e4654] = 你用拇指指甲刮掉青苔，把那些老字抄进笔记本。往山下面有人后来刻了一行很小的字：今年不行。你的指甲刮裂了。

@event lanes_well_dressing
# en: Dressing the Well
title [7fe79d] = 装点水井
# en: The mill village is dressing its well: a great picture in wet clay on a board, filled in petal by petal, every colour from the hedgerows. This year it's the harvest, sheaves and a sun, with a figure at the edge that nobody seems to want to name. An old woman hands you a basket of buttercups. "Every visitor puts in a petal," she says.
text [6a75fd] = 磨坊村在装点他们的井：一块板上抹着湿泥，拼成一幅大画，一片花瓣一片花瓣地填进去，树篱里有的颜色都在。今年画的是丰收，麦捆和太阳，画边上有一个人形，似乎谁都不愿意说出它的名字。一个老妇人递给你一篮毛茛。“每个来客都要放一片花瓣，”她说。
# en: A village well decorated with a huge picture made of pressed flower petals in clay, villagers adding petals, an old woman handing a student a basket of petals.
scene [8c5c14] = 一口乡村水井，装饰着一幅用压在泥里的花瓣拼成的巨画，村民们在添花瓣，一个老妇人把一篮花瓣递给一个学生。
# en: Put in your petals
opt.left.label [10f531] = 放上你的花瓣
# en: You press buttercups into the clay for an hour beside the villagers, who tell you where to put each one and correct you when you get it wrong. When it's done the picture glows. Your knees are stiff. The figure at the edge is the only part nobody let you touch.
opt.left.say.1 [7d08b8] = 你跪在村民旁边往泥里按了一个钟头毛茛，他们告诉你每一片该放在哪儿，放错了就纠正你。完成时画面熠熠生辉。你的膝盖僵了。画边上那个人形是唯一没人让你碰的部分。
# en: Ask who the figure is
opt.right.label [ffda3d] = 问那个人形是谁
# en: The old woman looks at the figure, and then at you, and smiles very warmly. "Oh, just somebody," she says, and goes back to her petals. Then she gives you a buttercup to put in its hand. You do. You can't say why your skin crawls.
opt.right.say.1 [e32a9d] = 老妇人看看那个人形，又看看你，笑得非常温暖。“哦，就是某个人，”她说，又低头弄她的花瓣。接着她给你一朵毛茛，让你放在它手里。你放了。你说不出为什么，浑身起了鸡皮疙瘩。

@event lanes_barn_owl
# en: The White Owl
title [b6d3ef] = 白色的猫头鹰
# en: A barn owl comes along the lane, low over the hedge, pale as paper and quite silent, and turns its white face to look at you as it passes. It lands on the gable of a ruined barn in the next field and waits there, as if it expected you to follow.
text [9744d2] = 一只仓鸮顺着小路飞来，低低地掠过树篱，白得像纸，一点声音也没有，经过时把白色的脸转过来看你。它落在旁边田里一座废弃谷仓的山墙上，在那儿等着，好像料定你会跟过去。
# en: A country lane at nightfall, a pale barn owl gliding low over the hedgerow, a ruined stone barn in a field beyond, a student watching.
scene [bb302e] = 夜幕降临时的乡间小路，一只苍白的仓鸮低低掠过树篱，远处田里一座废弃的石砌谷仓，一个学生在看。
# en: Follow it to the barn
opt.left.label [94c1a2] = 跟它去谷仓
# en: You cross the field in the half-dark and turn your ankle in a rabbit hole on the way. In the barn there are nests in every rafter, all empty, and the owl, watching you from the highest beam. You stand there under it a long while, and the air feels charged, like before a spell.
opt.left.say.1 [7afb40] = 你在半明半暗中穿过田野，路上一脚踩进兔子洞扭了脚踝。谷仓的每根椽子上都有巢，全是空的，那只猫头鹰在最高的横梁上看着你。你在它底下站了很久，空气里带着电，像施咒之前那样。
# en: Stand still and watch it hunt
opt.right.label [7c93c9] = 站着不动，看它捕猎
# en: You stand very still in the lane while it quarters the field in what light there is, once, twice, and drops into the grass like a falling sheet, and rises with something. It's the most beautiful thing you've seen all week.
opt.right.say.1 [086e20] = 你在小路上站得一动不动，借着仅有的一点光看它在田上来回巡了一遍、两遍，然后像一张落下的床单一样扎进草里，又带着什么东西飞起来。这是你这一星期看到的最美的东西。

@event lodging_doss_house_night
# en: A Night at the Doss-House
title [8a07ae] = 廉价客栈的一夜
# en: The doss-house is a long room of hammocks slung in rows, free to anyone, sleepers in their clothes, a smell of wet wool and a man by the door who snores like a saw. In the small hours you wake to a soft sound and see a thin shape creeping along the row, hand out, towards the boots under your hammock, where your purse is.
text [b76d2c] = 廉价客栈是一间长长的屋子，一排排挂着吊床，谁都能来睡，睡觉的人和衣而卧，一股湿羊毛味，门边一个男人打呼像拉锯。后半夜你被一声轻响惊醒，看见一个瘦削的影子沿着一排排吊床摸过来，手伸着，朝你吊床底下的靴子去，你的钱袋就在里面。
# en: A crowded doss-house dormitory at night, rows of slung hammocks, sleepers in their clothes, a thin figure creeping between the beds towards a student's boots.
scene [922a35] = 夜里拥挤的廉价客栈大通铺，一排排挂起的吊床，睡觉的人和衣而卧，一个瘦削的人影在吊床间悄悄朝一个学生的靴子摸去。
# en: Catch his wrist
opt.left.label [9a3e5f] = 抓住他的手腕
# en: You catch the wrist in the dark and hold on. It's a boy of eighteen or so, all bones, who stops struggling the moment he sees your face. You let him go, purse untouched, with a look he won't forget. He disappears. You lie awake, stiff and cold, till morning.
opt.left.say.1 [89f1e0] = 你在黑暗里抓住那只手腕，死死不放。是个十八九岁的男孩，瘦得只剩骨头，一看见你的脸就不挣扎了。你放了他，钱袋原封未动，只给了他一个他忘不掉的眼神。他不见了。你又冷又僵地醒着躺到天亮。
# en: You grab for the wrist and get a sleeve, and he twists out of it like an eel, purse and all, and is gone down the row. You bark your shin on the hammock-post going after him. Nobody in the room wakes up, or admits to it.
opt.left.say.2 [bba5ad] = 你去抓手腕，只抓到一只袖子，他像鳗鱼一样从袖子里滑脱，连钱袋一起，顺着那排吊床跑没了影。你追的时候小腿撞在吊床柱上。屋里谁也没醒，或者谁也不承认醒了。
# en: Roll over loudly
opt.right.label [32bba7] = 大声翻个身
# en: You roll over with a great snore and a kick, and the shape melts away down the row, to someone else's boots. In the morning a carter by the door is shouting about his purse. You don't look at him, and it sits on you all day.
opt.right.say.1 [f5a674] = 你打着大呼噜一翻身，顺带踢了一脚，那个影子便沿着那排吊床溜走了，去摸别人的靴子。早上门边一个赶车的在嚷嚷他的钱袋。你没看他，这事压在你心上一整天。

@event lodging_sailors_inn_night
# en: Songs at the Sailors' Inn
title [57b11a] = 水手客栈的歌
# en: Your room at the sailors' inn is over the taproom, and the taproom is singing. It's a ship's crew paid off today, and they're singing every song they know, and they know a great many, and they're getting to the ones about mermaids. The floor shakes with it. Sleep is not going to happen.
text [426f14] = 你在水手客栈的房间就在酒馆楼上，而酒馆在唱歌。一船水手今天领了工钱，正把会唱的歌全唱一遍，他们会的非常多，眼下唱到了美人鱼的那些。地板跟着震。觉是睡不成了。
# en: A low-beamed harbour inn at night, sailors singing around a table with tankards raised, a student in the doorway in a nightshirt.
scene [97ec93] = 低矮梁柱的港口客栈，夜里水手们围着桌子举杯唱歌，一个穿睡衣的学生站在门口。
# en: Go down and join them
opt.left.label [e5b28e] = 下楼加入他们
# en: You go down in your coat and they make room on the bench and teach you the chorus about the mermaid and the bosun, which has seventeen verses. You go to bed at dawn, hoarse and happy, and sleep through breakfast.
opt.left.say.1 [d7965e] = 你披上外套下楼，他们在长凳上给你腾出位置，教你唱美人鱼和水手长那首的副歌，一共十七段。你天亮才上床，嗓子哑了，心里高兴，一觉睡过了早饭。
# en: Bet them they can't sing quietly
opt.right.label [5ec357] = 跟他们打赌他们没法小声唱
# en: A coin on the table.
opt.right.hint [170159] = 在桌上押一枚硬币。
# en: You go down and bet the bosun a coin his crew can't sing the next one in a whisper. They can't, but they try, all of them, at the tops of their whispers, and it's so funny they give up singing altogether and pay up, your coin and theirs. You sleep.
opt.right.say.1 [abb6a6] = 你下楼跟水手长赌一枚硬币，说他的船员没法用耳语唱下一首。他们做不到，可他们全都试了，个个用最大的耳语，好笑得他们干脆不唱了，乖乖认输付钱，连你那枚一起还了。你睡着了。
# en: You bet the bosun a coin they can't sing in a whisper. They can, it turns out, beautifully, and then go straight back to roaring. The bosun pockets your coin, and you lie awake till dawn with the floor shaking.
opt.right.say.2 [149095] = 你跟水手长赌一枚硬币，说他们没法用耳语唱。结果他们能，唱得还非常好听，然后立刻又扯开嗓子吼起来。水手长把你的硬币揣进兜里，地板震着，你一直醒到天亮。

@event lodging_fine_room_night
# en: The Best Room in the House
title [540d7b] = 店里最好的房间
# en: The best room in the house has a bed with a canopy, a fire somebody else lit and a bell-pull by the pillow with a little brass card: RING FOR ANYTHING. It is very late. You look at the bell-pull. You have never in your life been allowed to ring for anything.
text [1f5af5] = 店里最好的房间有一张带华盖的床，一炉别人生好的火，枕边一根拉铃绳，挂着一张小铜牌：有事请拉铃。夜已经很深了。你看着那根拉铃绳。你这辈子还从没被允许为任何事拉过铃。
# en: A grand hotel bedroom at night, a canopied bed, a fire burning, a bell-pull by the bed, a porter at the door with a silver tray, a student in a dressing gown.
scene [05e14e] = 夜里一间豪华的旅馆卧室，一张带华盖的床，炉火在烧，床边一根拉铃绳，门口一个端着银托盘的侍者，一个穿晨衣的学生。
# en: Ring for supper
opt.left.label [95fe2f] = 拉铃要夜宵
# en: You ring. Ten minutes later a porter arrives with a silver tray: soup, a cold chicken, a slice of cake the size of a book and hot chocolate, all for the price of a week's bread. You eat it in bed in front of the fire, and feel, for one night, like a duke.
opt.left.say.1 [4eec86] = 你拉了铃。十分钟后一个侍者端着银托盘来了：汤、一只冷鸡、一块书那么大的蛋糕和热巧克力，价钱抵得上一星期的面包。你在床上对着炉火吃完了，有那么一晚，觉得自己像个公爵。
# en: Sleep in the great bed
opt.right.label [22c4aa] = 在大床上睡觉
# en: You sleep in the great canopied bed like a stone dropped in a well, and wake at noon to the fire relaid and a can of hot water steaming by the basin.
opt.right.say.1 [5ec294] = 你在那张带华盖的大床上睡得像一块扔进井里的石头，醒来已是中午，炉火重新生好了，脸盆边一罐热水冒着气。

@event lodging_hayloft_night
# en: A Night in the Hayloft
title [d2db9f] = 干草棚的一夜
# en: The hayloft costs nothing but a word with the farmer: warm hay, a slatted roof with moonlight coming through, a barn cat who considers you part of the arrangement. Towards midnight you wake to the cat sitting bolt upright, staring at the ladder. Something is coming up it, slowly, a rung at a time.
text [ffe878] = 干草棚只要跟农夫说一声就能睡，不花钱：暖和的干草，板条屋顶透进月光，一只谷仓猫认定你是这桩安排的一部分。快到半夜时你醒来，看见猫直挺挺地坐着，盯着梯子。有什么东西正顺着梯子往上爬，很慢，一级一级。
# en: A hayloft at night under a farm barn roof, moonlight through the slats, a student burrowed in the hay, a barn cat and an owl on a beam watching.
scene [34080e] = 夜里农场谷仓屋顶下的干草棚，月光从板条间透进来，一个学生钻在干草里，一只谷仓猫和横梁上的一只猫头鹰在看着。
# en: Look over the edge
opt.left.label [967f48] = 从边上往下看
# en: You look. It's the farmer's old dog, who has climbed the ladder to sleep beside the stranger because that's what she does. She lies down against your back with a groan. You don't get back to sleep, but you're warmer, and you scratched your arm on a nail looking.
opt.left.say.1 [bee268] = 你看了。是农夫家的老狗，它爬上梯子来睡在外乡人身边，因为它向来如此。它哼了一声，靠着你的背躺下了。你没再睡着，但暖和多了，而且往下看的时候胳膊被钉子划了一道。
# en: Pull the hay over your head
opt.right.label [cc269c] = 把干草拉过头顶
# en: You pull the hay over your head and wait. Whatever it is reaches the top of the ladder and stops there all night, breathing. In the morning there's nothing on the ladder but straw. You've lost the whole night's sleep, you ache from lying rigid, and you know now that a hayloft is never quite empty.
opt.right.say.1 [e7350e] = 你把干草拉过头顶，等着。不管那是什么，它爬到梯子顶上就停在那儿，喘了一整夜。早上梯子上除了干草什么也没有。你丢了一整夜的觉，僵着身子躺得浑身酸疼，也知道了干草棚从来不是完全空的。

@event lodging_inn_common_night
# en: The Inn's Common Room
title [69ccfd] = 客栈的公共厅
# en: Late in the coaching inn's common room the fire's burning down and an old drover is telling stories to whoever is still up: the high road in the old days, a highwayman who robbed only in rhyme, a winter when the river froze so hard they drove cattle over it. He looks over at you. "Do they tell stories at your castle?" he asks.
text [345892] = 驿站客栈的公共厅里夜已深了，炉火快熄了，一个老赶畜人在给还没睡的人讲故事：过去年月的大路，一个只用押韵的话打劫的拦路强盗，一个河冻得结结实实、能赶着牛走过去的冬天。他朝你看过来。“你们城堡里讲故事吗？”他问。
# en: A coaching inn's common room late at night, a dying fire, an old drover telling a story to a few guests, a student in a chair with a mug.
scene [b97ed5] = 深夜驿站客栈的公共厅，炉火将熄，一个老赶畜人在给几位客人讲故事，一个学生端着杯子坐在椅子上。
# en: Trade him a story
opt.left.label [a20261] = 跟他换个故事
# en: You tell him about a moving staircase and a cat who files the library, and he tells you about the highwayman in rhyme, and neither of you believes the other, and it's two in the morning before either of you notices. You're tired all the next day.
opt.left.say.1 [bd4788] = 你给他讲一座会动的楼梯和一只给图书馆归档的猫，他给你讲那个押韵的拦路强盗，两人谁也不信谁，等你们发觉，已经凌晨两点了。你第二天累了一整天。
# en: Go up early and sleep
opt.right.label [ea3789] = 早点上楼睡觉
# en: You say goodnight and go up while he's still talking. Through the floor you can hear him starting on the winter of the frozen river, and you fall asleep halfway through it, and wonder all the next day how it ended.
opt.right.say.1 [17b167] = 他还在讲，你道了晚安就上楼了。隔着地板你能听见他开始讲河冻住的那个冬天，你听到一半就睡着了，第二天一整天都在想它是怎么结尾的。

@event lodging_best_room_country_night
# en: The Feather Bed
title [13fac8] = 羽毛床
# en: The inn's best room has a feather bed so deep you sink to the ears, a jug of fresh milk by the bed and a window that looks out over the whole valley to the ridge, where the standing stones are black against the moon. Somebody has left a sprig of rowan on the pillow. Nobody at the inn knows anything about it.
text [8cde85] = 客栈最好的房间有一张深得能把你埋到耳朵的羽毛床，床边一罐鲜牛奶，窗户望出去是整个山谷，一直到山脊，立石在月光下黑黢黢的。有人在枕头上放了一枝花楸。客栈里谁也不知道是怎么回事。
# en: A coaching inn's best bedroom at night, a deep feather bed, a window looking out to a ridge of standing stones under the moon, a student at the window.
scene [c6e0dd] = 夜里驿站客栈最好的卧室，一张深深的羽毛床，窗外月光下是一道立着立石的山脊，一个学生站在窗边。
# en: Keep the rowan by you
opt.left.label [f3727a] = 把花楸放在身边
# en: You put the rowan under your pillow and sleep like the dead. Twice in the night you half wake to a sound at the window, like fingers on the glass. In the morning a wet reed from the marsh lies on the outside sill, two floors up, and the rowan has gone brown. You're uneasy all morning.
opt.left.say.1 [54fe1f] = 你把花楸放在枕头底下，睡得像死人一样。夜里两次你半醒过来，听见窗上有声音，像手指敲玻璃。早上，两层楼高的窗台外面躺着一根沼泽里的湿芦苇，花楸也变成了褐色。你一早上都心神不宁。
# en: Watch the stones a while
opt.right.label [096791] = 看一会儿那些石头
# en: You sit at the window with the milk and watch the stones on the ridge. Around midnight a light moves between them, slowly, stone to stone, and goes out. You sit up till dawn, waiting for it to come back. It doesn't. You're grey with tiredness all the next day.
opt.right.say.1 [2f01b7] = 你坐在窗边喝着牛奶，看着山脊上的石头。快到半夜时，一点光在石头之间慢慢移动，从一块到另一块，然后熄了。你一直坐到天亮等它回来。它没有。第二天你累得脸色发灰。
